noether 0.1
## Deutsch–Jozsa: decide with ONE oracle query whether f: {0,1}⁴ → {0,1} is constant or balanced.
##
## With the target in |−⟩ the oracle |x⟩|y⟩ → |x⟩|y ⊕ f(x)⟩ acts as the phase (−1)^{f(x)}, and
## after the final Hadamards
##     ⟨z|out⟩ = 2^{-n} Σ_x (−1)^{f(x) + z·x},   so   P(z = 0000) = |2^{-n} Σ_x (−1)^{f(x)}|²,
## which is 1 for a constant f and 0 for a balanced f.
##
## Oracles: f ≡ 0, f ≡ 1, and the balanced f(x) = x₀x₁ ⊕ x₂ (balanced because x₂ toggles it).
## For that f the sum factorises: only z with z₂ = 1, z₃ = 0 survive, each with |⟨z|out⟩| = 1/2,
## so P(0010) = P(0110) = P(1010) = P(1110) = 1/4 exactly. The target ends in |1⟩ every time.
## Sampling 2000 shots of the balanced case: never 0000, and each of the four outcomes
## 500 ± 19 (1σ), asserted ±75.
let n = 4
qubits x[n], y[1]; bits c[n]; seed 1
def ConstZero_{r[4],t}: I_t
def ConstOne_{r[4],t}: X_t
def Balanced_{r[4],t}: CNOT_{r[2]→t} Toffoli_{r[0], r[1]→t}
prepare |0000⟩ ⊗ |-⟩
H_x
ConstZero_{x, y[0]}
H_x; H_y
print |⟨00001|ψ⟩|^2 as pZeroConst0
assert |⟨00001|ψ⟩|^2 ≈ 1 ± 1e-12
prepare |0000⟩ ⊗ |-⟩
H_x
ConstOne_{x, y[0]}
H_x; H_y
print |⟨00001|ψ⟩|^2 as pZeroConst1
assert |⟨00001|ψ⟩|^2 ≈ 1 ± 1e-12
prepare |0000⟩ ⊗ |-⟩
H_x
Balanced_{x, y[0]}
H_x; H_y
print |⟨00001|ψ⟩|^2 as pZeroBalanced
assert |⟨00001|ψ⟩|^2 ≈ 0 ± 1e-12
assert |⟨00101|ψ⟩|^2 ≈ 1/4 ± 1e-12
assert |⟨01101|ψ⟩|^2 ≈ 1/4 ± 1e-12
assert |⟨10101|ψ⟩|^2 ≈ 1/4 ± 1e-12
assert |⟨11101|ψ⟩|^2 ≈ 1/4 ± 1e-12
c ← measure_x
counts ← run 2000
print counts
assert counts["0000"] == 0
assert counts["0010"] + counts["0110"] + counts["1010"] + counts["1110"] == 2000
assert counts["0010"] ≈ 500 ± 75
assert counts["1110"] ≈ 500 ± 75
